# Ignore everything except what's needed for the Vercel deploy
# (Flutter web build output + api/ serverless functions +
# assets/bibles JSON that the functions reference).
#
# Previous rewrite tried an allow-list approach with `*` at the top,
# but that filtered out api/*.js in ways I couldn't fully control —
# Vercel's `functions` config kept failing with "pattern api/**/*.js
# doesn't match any Serverless Functions". Deny-list is the proven
# recipe; just needs to be exhaustive.
.dart_tool
.idea
.gradle
android
ios
linux
macos
windows
test
lib
.git
*.dart
*.lock
.packages
.metadata
node_modules
.firebase
# Every build/<plugin> subtree can be huge and none of it needs to
# ship to Vercel. Xcode leaves "build/ios 2" DerivedData variants
# with broken symlinks that timed out the previous deploy. Only
# build/web needs to ship — ignore every other subdir and negate
# just web.
build/*
!build/web
